WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.958
The agency's cloud
decides what it can use,

2
00:00:02.958 --> 00:00:07.063
so the book dates every product
statement to October 2026.

3
00:00:07.063 --> 00:00:12.787
Microsoft announced the Agent ID platform,
with blueprints, agent identities and

4
00:00:12.787 --> 00:00:16.071
sponsors, as generally
available in April 2026,

5
00:00:16.071 --> 00:00:18.849
and sponsor lifecycle workflows in May.

6
00:00:18.849 --> 00:00:21.025
Several controls are still preview.

7
00:00:21.025 --> 00:00:25.927
The policy builder labels agent targeting
in Conditional Access as preview,

8
00:00:25.927 --> 00:00:30.599
agent identities support only Block,
the agent risk condition is preview,

9
00:00:30.599 --> 00:00:34.812
and agents' user accounts are
limited to Frontier program tenants.

10
00:00:34.812 --> 00:00:40.425
GCC has a partial, documented subset:
identity and access governance for agents,

11
00:00:40.425 --> 00:00:45.187
but not Microsoft's audit, data loss
prevention or network controls.

12
00:00:45.187 --> 00:00:48.473
GCC High and D O D have no
published availability,

13
00:00:48.473 --> 00:00:52.907
so treat agent identities as
unavailable there until Microsoft

14
00:00:52.907 --> 00:00:57.588
confirms otherwise in writing, and
govern AI as workload identities.

15
00:00:57.588 --> 00:01:02.275
And Agent 365's FedRAMP High
authorization is still pending.

16
00:01:02.275 --> 00:01:06.749
The program builds on what is generally
available in the agency's own cloud,

17
00:01:06.749 --> 00:01:09.340
and keeps preview features as watch items.
